                <pb facs="1122" n="1112" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.714/10–1849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-18T01:00:00+08:00">October 18, 1949—1
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:22 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1769. Note change October 1 of name Peiping to “Peking”. Believe conformity by
                    American Foreign Service establishments unobjectionable except on one point
                    Nationalist sensibilities, and conformity would avoid one minor point
                    exacerbation Communist feelings. Please instruct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
